[352.822772, "i", " 1000 has ratio 0.40 over cap 0.2, and stats are not stale.\",\n\"T-18 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because round-half-up raises the dead_pages/total_pages ratio from 0.205 to 0.21, which is over cap 0.2 for the large class computed from total_pages 1000.\",\n\"T-20 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum even though enabled; the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.10 under cap 0.2, but the manual vacuum override is checked first.\",\n\"T-29 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because its reindex approval expired on 2026-08-25, so bloat applies; the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.25 over cap 0.2.\",\n\"T-35 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 500 computes a large class with cap 0.2, and ratio 0.22 is over that cap.\",\n\"T-37 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because its reindex approval expired on 2026-08-25, so bloat applies; the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.25 over cap 0.2.\",\n\"T-39 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum over"]
[352.823011, "o", "health_path = '/app/input/table_health.csv'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[352.823256, "i", "rides autovacuum even though enabled; the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.05 under cap 0.2, but the manual vacuum override is checked first.\",\n\"T-44 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because the export medium trap is ignored and the computed large class comes from total_pages 600 with cap 0.2, so ratio 0.83 is over the cap.\",\n\"T-08 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.45 over cap 0.2, with no stale stats or reindex exemption.\",\n\"T-02 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.35 over cap 0.2, and stats are not stale.\",\n\"T-03 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum_enabled is false and checked first; the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.15 under cap 0.2, but the disabled autovacuum overrides.\",\n\"T-05 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because its reindex is unapproved, so bloat applies; the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.55 over cap 0.2.\",\n\"T-11"]
[352.823489, "i", " is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum_enabled is false and checked first; the large class computed from total_pages 1000 has ratio 0.41 over cap 0.2, but the disabled autovacuum overrides.\",\n]\n\nmemo = \"# Bloat Maintenance Memo\\n\\n\"\nmemo += \"The audit computes bloat_ratio as dead_pages/total_pages with round-half-up to two decimals, computes size_class from total_pages, and ignores the export size_class column including the medium trap. Autovacuum is checked first, bloat is checked next with stale-statistics cap tightening, and stale statistics are checked last.\\n\\n\"\nmemo += \"## Non-compliant findings\\n\\n\"\nfor b in bullets:\n    memo += \"- \" + b + \"\\n\"\nmemo += \"\\n## Active reindex and cap-equality notes\\n\\n\"\nmemo += \"- T-28 has an approved active reindex valid through 2026-09-15, so its bloat ratio 0.25 over cap 0.2 is exempt and the finding is none.\\n\"\nmemo += \"- A computed ratio exactly equaling its size-class cap is compliant because the policy uses strictly greater than; thus T-12, T-15, T-32, T-34, an"]
[352.823912, "i", "d T-41 are none, while T-42 is not because stale stats tighten its cap.\\n\"\n\nwith open('/app/bloat_memo.md', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(memo)\nPY\n"]
[352.824529, "o", "reindex_path = '/app/input/reindex_log.csv'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[352.824957, "o", "reidx = {}\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[352.825693, "o", "with open(reindex_path, newline='') as f:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[352.825845, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[352.826573, "o", "    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[352.82691, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[352.827578, "o", "        reidx[r['table_name']] = r\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
